One focus of the ellipse $\frac{x^2}{2} + y^2 = 1$ is at $F = (1,0).$  There exists a point $P = (p,0),$ where $p > 0,$ such that for any chord $\overline{AB}$ that passes through $F,$ angles $\angle APF$ and $\angle BPF$ are equal.  Find $p.$

[asy]
unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, F, P;
path ell = xscale(sqrt(2))*Circle((0,0),1);

F = (1,0);
A = (sqrt(2)*Cos(80),Sin(80));
B = intersectionpoint(interp(A,F,0.1)--interp(A,F,5),ell);
P = (2,0);

draw(ell);
draw(A--B);
draw(A--P--B);
draw(F--P);

dot("$A$", A, N);
dot("$B$", B, SE);
dot("$F$", F, SW);
dot("$P$", P, E);
[/asy]

Let $\overline{AD},$ $\overline{BE},$ $\overline{CF}$ be the altitudes of acute triangle $ABC.$  If
\[9 \overrightarrow{AD} + 4 \overrightarrow{BE} + 7 \overrightarrow{CF} = \mathbf{0},\]then compute $\angle ACB,$ in degrees.

[asy]
unitsize (0.6 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, H;

A = (2,5);
B = (0,0);
C = (8,0);
D = (A + reflect(B,C)*(A))/2;
E = (B + reflect(C,A)*(B))/2;
F = (C + reflect(A,B)*(C))/2;

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D);
draw(B--E);
draw(C--F);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SW);
label("$C$", C, SE);
label("$D$", D, S);
label("$E$", E, NE);
label("$F$", F, NW);
[/asy]

